PROMETHEUS
===============================================================================

Q1. What is Prometheus?

Answer

Prometheus is an Open Source Monitoring and Alerting Tool developed by
SoundCloud and maintained by CNCF.

It collects metrics from servers, stores them in TSDB and evaluates alert rules.

-------------------------------------------------------------------------------

Q2. What is TSDB?

Answer

TSDB means Time Series Database.

Stores

Metric

+

Timestamp

+

Value

-------------------------------------------------------------------------------

Q3. What is PromQL?

Answer

PromQL is Prometheus Query Language used for querying metrics.

-------------------------------------------------------------------------------

Q4. Prometheus Push or Pull?

Answer

Pull.

Prometheus itself scrapes metrics from exporters.

-------------------------------------------------------------------------------

Q5. Default Port?

Answer

9090

-------------------------------------------------------------------------------

Q6. Prometheus Configuration File?

Answer

/etc/prometheus/prometheus.yml

-------------------------------------------------------------------------------

Q7. How to validate configuration?

Answer

promtool check config /etc/prometheus/prometheus.yml

-------------------------------------------------------------------------------

Q8. How to restart Prometheus?

Answer

systemctl restart prometheus

-------------------------------------------------------------------------------

Q9. How to check logs?

Answer

journalctl -u prometheus -f

-------------------------------------------------------------------------------

Q10. Where can you check Targets?

Answer

http://server:9090/targets

